 "reading": [
  "8,192 steps: the policy drives and never arrives; this only proves the interface works.",
  "60,000 steps on all 40 goals: still 0/9, but the mean final distance fell from 3.12 m to 1.66 m and the mean path from 4.85 m to 2.49 m, so it learned to approach.  Contact episodes disappear in the last 20k steps while arrivals stay near 10%.",
  "20,000 steps on the nearest 8 goals: 0/8 on the very goals it trained on, with a mean final distance of 0.864 m.  A trace shows the vehicle driving to 0.679 m from the goal and then commanding zero for the rest of the episode -- stopping beat risking the last metre, because contact costs -5.0 and idling costs -0.01 per step.",
  "Charging 0.03 per metre of remaining distance every step removes that trap: the same budget and goal pool goes from 0/8 to 4/8 with a mean final distance of 0.613 m.  The fixed goals and the held-out goals stay at zero, so finishing a practised goal and generalising are separate problems and only the first was fixed.",
  "Returns are not comparable across the reward variants: the distance charge lowers the return of a successful episode from about +5.9 to +2.8, so arrival counts must be compared, not mean return."
